111. GRANT
GRANT is used to provide previleegs (permissions) to users.
Giving all permissions to users for all databases and tables                              - grant all privileges on *.* to user_name@localhost;
Giving only select and update permissions to users for all databases and tables           -  grant select,update  on *.* to user_name@localhost;
Giving only select and update permissions to users for only particular database and table - grant select,update  on database_name.table_name to user_name@localhost;

112. REVOKE
REVOKE – Removes access privileges(permissions)  from users 
removing all permissions from users for all databases and tables                  - revoke all privileges on *.* from user_name@localhost;
Removing only drop and select permissions from users for all databases and tables - Revoke drop,select on *.* from user_name@localhost;
Removing all permissions from users for only selected database and tables         - Revoke all privileges on database_name.table_name from user_name@localhost;

113. Backup and Restore
Backup saves database copies. Restore recovers them.
A copy of data that you can use to restore and recover the data after a failure.

BACKUP DATABASE YourDatabaseName
TO DISK = 'C:\Backups\YourDatabaseName.bak'
WITH FORMAT, MEDIANAME = 'SQLServerBackups', NAME = 'Full Backup of YourDatabaseName';


RESTORE DATABASE YourDatabaseName
FROM DISK = 'C:\Backups\YourDatabaseName.bak'
WITH REPLACE;


